{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"garbage mattes for key extraction garbage mattes for key extraction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","fileName":"Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Compositing and Keying]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Compositing and Keying","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"garbage mattes for key extraction garbage mattes for key extraction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","fileName":"Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction","heading":"Garbage Mattes for Key Extraction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A garbage matte quickly removes portions of a shot that lie well outside the subject before a fine key is attempted. It need not follow every hair or moving contour; it only reduces the area where the keyer must distinguish the subject from its screen. A narrow band of screen can remain near the subject for the key to resolve. In the book's crowd-shadow example, a roto garbage matte first isolates the performer before the blue-screen key is pulled. This coarse-to-fine division saves detailed keying work.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Compositing and Keying","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":